                  <provenance type="#i"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_496">Sheen, Surrey.
                        Charterhouse of Jesus of Bethlehem</orgName><p>Cambridge, Emmanuel
                        College, MS 35, Trinity College, MS 345, and the Hilton in Philadelphia
                        contain notes in the hand of James Grenehalgh (professed 1495). Grenehalgh
                        also annotated Bodl. MS Douce 262 (see under London, Charterhouse), BL MS
                        Royal 5 A. v (see under Coventry, Charterhouse) and his monogram is in BL
                        MSS Add. 24461 and 37790 and probably Harley 2373 (see under Mount
                        Grace).</p><p>Colophon says: 'Scriptum quidem est hoc opus per Beuet quondam
                        procuratorem in Carthusia de Schen super Tamisiam Quod Grenehalgh eiusdem
                        domus professus indigna manu sua In festo Reliquiarum fe. 6a. sero 1499.',
                        cf. H. E. Allen, Writings ascr. to R. Rolle, p. 216.</p><p>Monogram of 'J.
                        G.'.</p><p> </p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">A note mentions St Giles's,
                     Norwich.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">On fol. 115v Henry Brereton (s.
                     xvi).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Given to Trinity by George Willmer (d.
                     1626).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners"> </provenance>
               </history>
